    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$1686.85$ every 6 months.",
      "worked": "There are $4\\times2=8$ six-monthly periods, with interest of $6\\%\\div2=3\\%$ per period. The future value table gives a factor of $8.8923$. Let $M$ be the deposit each 6 months.\n$$\\begin{align*}FV&=\\text{FV of }\\$1\\times M\\\\15\\,000&=8.8923M\\\\M&=\\frac{15\\,000}{8.8923}\\\\M&\\approx\\$1686.85\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
